      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9518c3f8-4f14-5db8-9a4a-cfefa492a6d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gioachino Rossini, Andrea Leone Tottola, Francesco Ringhieri, Gaetano Donizetti, Sonia Ganassi, Richard Mohr, Samuel Barber, Gian Carlo Menotti\n- Works: Mosè in Egitto, Lucrezia Borgia, L'Osiride, Vanessa, Amahl and the Night Visitors, Ernani, Luisa Miller, Rigoletto, Aida, La Traviata, Il Trovatore, Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra, La donna del lago, Ermione\n- Organizations/Events: ROF, Rossini in Wildbad\n- Concepts: opera recordings, world premieres, first LP recordings\n\nFacts:\n- Francesco Ringhieri wrote the 1760 play L'Osiride.\n- Gioachino Rossini wrote the three-act opera Mosè in Egitto to an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola, and the opera was based on Francesco Ringhieri's 1760 play L'Osiride.\n- Gaetano Donizetti composed Lucrezia Borgia as a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts.\n- Sonia Ganassi performed Rossini roles including Elisabetta in Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra at ROF in 2004.\n- Sonia Ganassi performed Elena in La donna del lago at Rossini in Wildbad in 2006.\n- Sonia Ganassi performed in Ermione at ROF in 2008.\n- Sonia Ganassi performed Elcia in Mosè in Egitto at ROF in 2011.\n- Richard Mohr produced recordings of the casts of the world premieres of Samuel Barber's Vanessa and Gian Carlo Menotti's Amahl and the Night Visitors.\n- Richard Mohr also produced the first LP recordings of Ernani, Luisa Miller, and Lucrezia Borgia, as well as three versions each of Rigoletto, Aida, La Traviata, and Il Trovatore.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e91f9b37-c7c8-562a-b333-97c331d577db",
        "text": "Page: Mosè in Egitto. Sentence: Mosè in Egitto (\"Moses in Egypt)\" (] ) is a three-act opera written by Gioachino Rossini to an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola, which was based on a 1760 play by Francesco Ringhieri, \"L'Osiride\".\nPage: Lucrezia Borgia (opera). Sentence: Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\nPage: Sonia Ganassi. Sentence: Her roles in Rossini operas include Elisabetta in \"Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra\" (ROF, 2004), Elena in \"La donna del lago (Lady of the Lake)\" (Rossini in Wildbad, 2006), \"Ermione\" (ROF, 2008), and Elcia in \"Mosè in Egitto\" (ROF, 2011).\nPage: Richard Mohr. Sentence: His producing credits included recording the casts of the world premieres of Samuel Barber's \"Vanessa\" and Gian Carlo Menotti's \"Amahl and the Night Visitors,\" as well as the first LP recordings of \"Ernani,\" \"Luisa Miller\" and \"Lucrezia Borgia\" and three versions each of \"Rigoletto,\" \"Aida,\" \"La Traviata\" and \"Il Trovatore.\"",
